ernalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067944230","verified_at":"2026-10-21T00:38:14Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5308630-1846018067931506","game_id":"steam-5308630","kind":"announcement","title":"Devlog 8 - Flinging cat shit puzzle!","summary":"Come on! Surely there must be another game out there with a cat that throws shit at you if you don't run away from it?! Well, if there's not, then this will be a first. I proudly present to you a compilation of the possible outcomes of the cat-shit-flinging puzzle. Originally posted on the A Beacon devlog.","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-08T21:52:54Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067931506","verified_at":"2026-10-21T00:38:14Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5308630-1845383656396491","game_id":"steam-5308630","kind":"announcement","title":"Devlog 7 - The Cave of the Cats","summary":"Where are you going with this? Well, you might well ask. One of the many things ‘A Beacon’ will include is quite a lot of folklore, some of it borrowed from outside Staffordshire and relating to my Irish heritage. One such tale is the Cave of the Cats in Connaught, Ireland. It’s a site with mysterious earthworks and underground passages that has only recently been surveyed with electronic scanning. Some say these caves lead to other realms. Further reading on the Cave of the Cats So, without giv","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-06T13:48:24Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1845383656396491","verified_at":"2026-10-21T00:38:14Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5308630":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T09:31:42Z","status":"ok","all_sou